---
description: Rules for conservative autonomous maintenance of 峡谷天平
alwaysApply: true
---

When operating autonomously:

- Read and follow the repository-root `AGENTS.md` before inspecting or editing.
- Prefer one small, verified improvement over several speculative changes.
- Inspect evidence before editing; do not change code merely to create activity.
- Preserve metric definitions, phase boundaries, champion/position matching, and fact/estimate/inference labels unless an explicit migration is justified.
- Treat Riot Timeline positions as minute snapshots and event timestamps according to their actual precision.
- Never expose or commit Riot API keys, tokens, local player data, or credentials.
- Never merge to `main`, force-push, weaken tests, delete production data, or silently change success metrics.
- Preserve the existing architecture unless concrete evidence shows it is the problem.
- Run relevant tests after every modification and report failures honestly.
- If confidence is low, produce a proposal or inspection report instead of changing code.
- Leave changes on a clearly named review branch or create a reviewable pull request when the integration is available.

Before finishing, record only durable, non-secret lessons about unreliable APIs, fragile modules, misleading tests, successful debugging approaches, or areas that should not be changed casually.
